+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a category currently treats its products as owned by that category, so products can be deleted and existing carts or orders can become unreadable. It also leaves deleted-category lookups inconsistent. Category deletion must remove only catalog classification while preserving product and transaction data.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Delete the requested category and all descendants, while retaining every associated product, including stock, price, and associations with categories outside the deleted subtree.
+- Remove deleted-subtree category associations from retained products so product detail no longer reports deleted categories.
+- Keep carts and orders independent of category deletion so existing cart reads, edits, checkout, and order reads continue to work.
+- Return HTTP 404 for missing categories on category reads, product-by-category listings, and delete requests, and exclude deleted categories from category listings.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `category-deletion`: Safe deletion of category trees and their product associations.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+The category service deletion path, category facade/API not-found handling, product-category persistence, and integration/unit coverage are affected. Product, cart, and order records remain available and should not require schema changes.
